  "description": "ZESFIQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H68 Cl4 Dy6 N8 O26 S2 2+,4(C1 H4 O1),2(Cl1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.523-3.746 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.11-109.13°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(L4)4(L5)2(μ3-OH)4(CH3O)4Cl4]Cl2 (H2L4 = 2-hydroxy-3-methoxybenzaldehyde; H2L5 = 2-(((5-amino-1,3,4-thiadiazol-2-yl)amino)(hydroxy)methyl)-6-methoxyphenol). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
